## 4. Data Model

### 4.1 Table: `categories`

Stores income/expense categories used for budget items.

| Field | Type                  | Description                             |
| ----- | --------------------- | --------------------------------------- |
| id    | PK                    | unique id                               |
| name  | string                | e.g. Rent, Salary                       |
| type  | enum("INCOME","EXPENSE") | category type                           |
| rank  | int                   | ordering for display (lower = earlier) |

---

### 4.2 Table: `persons`

Stores people for shared budgets.

| Field | Type   | Description |
| ----- | ------ | ----------- |
| id    | PK     | unique id   |
| name  | string | display name|

---

### 4.3 Table: `budget_items`

Stores every recurring payment once.

| Field       | Type                              | Description                    |
| ----------- | --------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |
| id          | PK                                | unique id                      |
| type        | enum("INCOME","EXPENSE")          | item direction                 |
| name        | string                            | e.g. Rent, Salary              |
| category_id | FK                                | → categories.id                |
| person_id   | FK/null                           | → persons.id (null = shared)   |
| amount      | decimal                           | always positive                |
| frequency   | enum("MONTHLY","ONE_TIME","QUARTERLY","HALF_YEARLY","YEARLY") | recurrence pattern |
| start_date  | date                              | start date                     |
| end_date    | date/null                         | optional end date              |
| active      | boolean                           | included in calculations       |
| planned     | boolean                           | planned vs actual item         |

> **Note:**
> Sign is not stored — direction is defined via `type`. Planned items (`planned = true`) are regular recurring items; actual items (`planned = false`) represent month overrides.

